A 2-buffer pool starves the capture loop: Chromium/Electron consumers hold both
buffers while encoding, so xdpw hits "out of buffers", drops the frame and falls
back to the retry timer, collapsing a 30fps screencast to ~1-18fps. Raise the
floor so the consumer can hold two and the compositor still has one to write.

Upstream https://github.com/emersion/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr/pull/396

diff --git a/include/pipewire_screencast.h b/include/pipewire_screencast.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/include/pipewire_screencast.h
+++ b/include/pipewire_screencast.h
@@ -3,8 +3,8 @@

 #include "screencast_common.h"

-#define XDPW_PWR_BUFFERS 2
-#define XDPW_PWR_BUFFERS_MIN 2
+#define XDPW_PWR_BUFFERS 8
+#define XDPW_PWR_BUFFERS_MIN 4
 #define XDPW_PWR_ALIGN 16

 void xdpw_pwr_enqueue_buffer(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast);
